# §35 — CREDENTIALS. `Admin Accounts/` held a live Twilio 2FA recovery code that was
# tracked in Git (removed from the index 2026-09-14; it still exists in PAST commits,
# so the code must be treated as COMPROMISED and ROTATED). Never track this folder.
Admin Accounts/
Random/

# ── GENERATED ARTEFACTS — NEVER TRACKED (clean-slate reconciliation 2026-09-21) ──
# These are REPRODUCIBLE OUTPUTS of a test/export run, not source. They were tracked
# until 2026-09-21, which made `git status` dirty after EVERY Playwright run (117
# screenshot binaries + the 61 MB review zip rewritten each session) and made a clean
# checkpoint impossible. They stay on disk; they are simply not versioned.
# `scripts/validate-e6-brand-surfaces.mjs` already ignores these as GENERATED_ARTEFACTS.
test-screenshots/
forensic-captures/
playwright-report/
test-results/
e2e-report/
# §E2E-8 (2026-10-08) — ignore EVERYTHING under `Review Zip/` except the one file
# that is deliberately tracked. The previous rule (`Review Zip/*.zip` only) let a
# binder's own transient temp file (Info-ZIP creates `ziXXXXXX` beside the archive
# while it builds) be committed by `git add -A`. `git` never reads the export
# script, so the ignore must be broad enough on its own.
Review Zip/*
!Review Zip/INCIDENT-LOG.md

# ── §Wave 3 — RAW GEOGRAPHY DATASET CACHE (NEVER TRACKED) ─────────────────────
# `scripts/build-logistics-hero-geo.mjs` downloads the authoritative datasets
# (Natural Earth, ~13 MB; OpenStreetMap UK roads via Overpass, ~14 MB) so they
# can be simplified into the COMMITTED `src/data/logisticsHeroGeo.ts`. The raw
# multi-megabyte downloads are build inputs, not source: they are reproducible
# with `npm run build:hero-geo -- --fetch` and must never be versioned.
.geo-cache/

